integ5 0091 = patches/attn5/0070-glm-decode-index-scores-on-glm-index-scores.patch (overnight 2026-10-31), renumbered for the integrated stack on 3f94715d.

attn5 0070 (c4, overnight 2026-10-31): a decode window's DSA index scores on glm_index_scores, exact.
Applies after 0067 (and 0068, 0069) on 3f94715d.

A decode window's rows (under 64, 16-byte aligned key cache) take tf_glm_index_scores (glm_index's scores kernel, 8 rows
a CTA, 16 key tiles of 64 pools a CTA, double-buffered: each key tile staged once for the window's rows) instead of
tf_glm_scores (a CTA a row and 64-pool block, q staged again for every block). The kernel is tf_glm_scores' arithmetic
bit for bit (glm-index-check compares them). Prompt chunks keep TF_GLM_INDEX_CUDA's rule. The glm_index module now
loads always unless TF_GLM_DSCORES=0 (then decode windows keep tf_glm_scores; a warn line says so; a typo is refused).
Checks: attn5/bench/scorebench byte-compares the two kernels' written columns at 128K/200K/512K/864K x 1/4/16 rows;
glm-index-check's decode section compares selectTokens with today's set against dsel + dscore (scores, pools, lists,
counts); test-glm-index-host (takesDecode rule).

